g them gain little over the best single), suggesting they load on a shared underlying factor. If that factor decays out-of-sample, the whole family degrades together \u2014 the downside tail here is correlated, not diversified away.\n\nSeparately: several claude.ai MCP connectors (Gmail, Google Drive, Linear, and ~35 others) reported needing OAuth authorization. This session is non-interactive so I couldn't run that flow, but none of it was needed \u2014 `evaluate` and `submit` worked throughout. If you want those connectors available later, they'd need authorizing via claude.ai connector settings, or `claude mcp` / `/mcp` in an interactive session."}
